- description: Kubernetes Utilization measures the efficiency of resource usage within Kubernetes clusters, specifically focusing on nodes and pods. This metric evaluates how effectively CPU and memory resources are allocated and consumed by running applications. High utilization indicates that resources are being used efficiently, while low utilization may suggest over-provisioning or underutilization of resources. The scope of this metric includes all active nodes and pods within the cluster, providing insights into workload distribution and resource optimization. Monitoring this metric helps organizations identify opportunities for scaling, cost reduction, and improved performance.

