Metric:
- id: scaling.effectiveness
- name: Scaling Effectiveness
- description: Scaling Effectiveness measures the responsiveness and appropriateness of autoscaling actions in relation to the actual workload demands on cloud resources. It evaluates how quickly and accurately the system can adjust its capacity—either scaling up or down—to meet the target load without causing performance degradation or resource wastage. This metric focuses on the timing of scaling events, ensuring that resources are provisioned or decommissioned in a timely manner to match fluctuations in demand. Additionally, it assesses whether the scaling actions taken are sufficient to handle the load, preventing bottlenecks or over-provisioning. By analyzing this metric, organizations can optimize their cloud resource utilization, enhance application performance, and manage costs effectively.

