Metric:
- id: lb.performance
- name: Load Balancer Performance
- description: This metric measures the performance of load balancers by analyzing request latency and error rates in relation to established Service Level Objectives (SLOs). It provides insights into how efficiently the load balancer is distributing incoming traffic across backend servers, which is crucial for maintaining application responsiveness. High request latency may indicate bottlenecks or misconfigurations, while elevated error rates can signal issues with backend services or network connectivity. By comparing these metrics against SLOs, organizations can assess whether their load balancing strategy meets performance expectations. This metric is essential for ensuring optimal user experience and operational reliability.

