Metric:
- id: storage.efficiency
- name: Storage Efficiency
- description: Storage Efficiency measures the amount of avoidable or wasteful capacity within a cloud storage environment. This includes identifying unattached volumes, orphaned resources, and stale hot-tier data that are no longer actively used but still incur costs. By quantifying these inefficiencies, organizations can gain insights into their storage utilization and identify opportunities for optimization. The metric helps in assessing the effectiveness of storage management practices and informs decisions on resource allocation. Ultimately, improving storage efficiency contributes to cost savings and enhances overall cloud resource management.

