Metric:
- id: cost.idle_underutilized
- name: Cost – Idle/Underutilized
- description: This metric measures the proportion of cloud spending that is associated with resources that are either idle or underutilized. Idle resources are those that are provisioned but not actively being used, while underutilized resources are those that are being used below their capacity. By quantifying this cost, organizations can identify inefficiencies in their cloud infrastructure and optimize resource allocation. The scope of this metric includes all types of cloud resources, such as virtual machines, storage, and databases, across various cloud service providers. Understanding idle and underutilized costs is crucial for effective FinOps practices, enabling organizations to reduce waste and improve overall cloud cost management.

