Metric:
- id: cost.allocation_quality
- name: Cost – Allocation Quality
- description: The Cost – Allocation Quality metric measures the accuracy and appropriateness of cloud spending attribution to various teams and services within an organization. It evaluates how well cloud costs are distributed based on actual usage and resource consumption, ensuring that each team or service is charged fairly for the resources they utilize. This metric is crucial for effective financial management and accountability, as it directly impacts budgeting and forecasting processes. High allocation quality indicates that the organization has robust tagging and resource management practices in place, while low quality may suggest misattribution or lack of visibility into resource usage. Ultimately, this metric helps organizations optimize their cloud spending and align costs with business objectives.

