- description: This metric measures the degree to which sensitive services within a cloud infrastructure are exposed to the public internet. It assesses the presence of open ingress points, such as unsecured APIs or ports, as well as the configuration of public storage buckets and public IP addresses. A higher degree of public exposure indicates a greater risk of unauthorized access and potential data breaches. The scope includes all assets that can be accessed externally, focusing on their security configurations. By monitoring this metric, organizations can identify vulnerabilities and take necessary actions to enhance their security posture.

