Metric:
- id: security.vuln_patch
- name: Security – Vulnerability & Patch Hygiene
- description: This metric measures the effectiveness of an organization's vulnerability management and patching processes. It specifically tracks the backlog of identified vulnerabilities across the cloud infrastructure and assesses the timeliness of patch deployments against established Service Level Agreements (SLAs). A high vulnerability backlog may indicate insufficient resources or prioritization in addressing security risks, while timely patching reflects an organization's responsiveness to emerging threats. The scope includes all cloud assets, ensuring comprehensive coverage of both virtual and physical resources. By monitoring this metric, organizations can enhance their security posture and reduce the risk of exploitation from unpatched vulnerabilities.

